    "topic": "where the word guy comes from",
    "summary": "'Guy' comes from Guy Fawkes, caught guarding the gunpowder in the 1605 plot to blow up the House of Lords and kill King James. Children's effigies of him burned on 5 November were called guys; by 1845 a guy was an oddly dressed person, and by 1873 any man.",
